26n0|n|The front of an army; the first line or leading column; also, the front line or foremost division of a fleet, either in sailing or in battle. ; A shovel used in cleansing ore. ; A light wagon, either covered or open, used by tradesmen and others fore the transportation of goods. ; A large covered wagon for moving furniture, etc., also for conveying wild beasts, etc., for exhibition. ; A close railway car for baggage. See the Note under Car, 2. ; A fan or other contrivance, as a sieve, for winnowing grain. ; A wing with which the air is beaten.	a:1qxu,150,2;ad0,107,2;13o3,98,1;1qpy,82,4;22mq,77,3;1713,63,1;7md,20,3;1dub,16,4~1qpy,82,4;1dub,16,4;7md,20,3;22mq,77,3;1qxu,150,2;ad0,107,2;1713,63,1;13o3,98,1	v:22mq,61,1~22mq,61,1	V:28x3,132,2;iux,79,1~28x3,132,2;iux,79,1	n:1qxu,150,2;13o3,98,1;4li,97,9;ad0,97,1;1qpy,85,5;22mq,71,2;1i2o,67,2;iol,66,4;8l6,60,1;hqf,60,1;r5b,59,1;13m9,51,2;1pj5,25,2;224y,11,5;277w,10,3~4li,97,9;1qpy,85,5;224y,11,5;iol,66,4;277w,10,3;1pj5,25,2;22mq,71,2;1qxu,150,2;1bsr,0,2;1i2o,67,2;13m9,51,2;ad0,97,1;8l6,60,1;r5b,59,1;hqf,60,1	N:28x3,152,8;mp8,130,2;1h8s,123,1;n34,116,2;16sy,116,1;xon,110,2;iux,107,7;idj,89,17;mbf,24,6~idj,89,17;28x3,152,8;iux,107,7;mbf,24,6;mp8,130,2;n34,116,2;xon,110,2;1h8s,123,1;16sy,116,1
