26nd|n|A contrivance attached to some elevated object for the purpose of showing which way the wind blows; a weathercock. It is usually a plate or strip of metal, or slip of wood, often cut into some fanciful form, and placed upon a perpendicular axis around which it moves freely. ; Any flat, extended surface attached to an axis and moved by the wind; as, the vane of a windmill; hence, a similar fixture of any form moved in or by water, air, or other fluid; as, the vane of a screw propeller, a fan blower, an anemometer, etc. ; The rhachis and web of a feather taken together. ; One of the sights of a compass, quadrant, etc.	a:1hai,154,6;fka,121,3;1r2f,97,4;1xk6,83,4;w4k,50,4;1tjh,46,3;1uus,20,2~1hai,154,6;1r2f,97,4;1xk6,83,4;w4k,50,4;1tjh,46,3;fka,121,3;1uus,20,2	v:282v,42,4~282v,42,4	n:11t4,86,3;ecb,75,3;2bz,75,7;1m2t,71,4;24au,70,3;5bv,65,5;28aa,61,4;28vf,54,4;w4k,40,2;282v,22,1;1uus,10,1;1zml,8,1~2bz,75,7;5bv,65,5;28aa,61,4;1m2t,71,4;28vf,54,4;ecb,75,3;24au,70,3;11t4,86,3;w4k,40,2;282v,22,1;1uus,10,1;1zml,8,1	N:1uh6,96,1;33w,71,4;33s,44,3;26hk,29,3;20f9,8,4;296v,5,3~33w,71,4;20f9,8,4;296v,5,3;33s,44,3;26hk,29,3;1uh6,96,1
